{
  "title": "Adjectives: colors, sizes, and endings that tag along",
  "title_target": "У магазині одягу — U mahazyni odyahu",
  "goal": "Describe things with adjectives whose endings match, name colors, and shop for clothes from browsing to paying.",
  "bekal": [
    "match adjective endings to the noun's gender",
    "name twelve colors",
    "ask with Який, Яка, Яке, Які",
    "ask for another size and try clothes on",
    "describe people and things"
  ],
  "dialogs": [
    {
      "title": "Діалог — A sweater for the first winter",
      "intro": "Ani goes clothes shopping before winter. Notice that every adjective changes its ending to match the thing it describes, and that the same thing gets a different ending once it becomes the object of an action.",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "Продавчиня:",
          "text": "[Доброго|DOB-ro-ho] [дня|dnya]! [Вам|Vam] [допомогти|do-po-moh-TI]?",
          "id": "Good afternoon! Can I help you?",
          "literal": "good — day! to-you — to-help?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Ані:",
          "text": "[Так|Tak]. [Я|Ya] [шукаю|shoo-KA-yoo] [светр|svetr].",
          "id": "Yes. I'm looking for a sweater.",
          "literal": "yes. I — look-for — sweater."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Продавчиня:",
          "text": "[Який|Ya-KIY] [колір|KO-leer] [ви|vi] [хочете|KHO-cheh-teh]?",
          "id": "What color would you like?",
          "literal": "which (m) — color — you — want?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Ані:",
          "text": "[Синій|SI-neey] [або|A-bo] [зелений|zeh-LEH-niy].",
          "id": "Blue or green.",
          "literal": "blue — or — green."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Продавчиня:",
          "text": "[Ось|Os'] [синій|SI-neey]. [Це|Tseh] [ваш|vash] [розмір|ROZ-meer]?",
          "id": "Here's a blue one. Is this your size?",
          "literal": "here-is — blue. this — your — size?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Ані:",
          "text": "[Здається|Zda-YEH-tsya], [великий|veh-LI-kiy]. [Є|Yeh] [менший|MEN-shiy]?",
          "id": "I think it's too big. Is there a smaller one?",
          "literal": "it-seems, big. is-there — smaller?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Продавчиня:",
          "text": "[Є|Yeh]. [Ось|Os'] [цей|tsey].",
          "id": "Yes. Here you go.",
          "literal": "there-is. here-is — this-one (m)."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Ані:",
          "text": "[Можна|MOZH-na] [поміряти|po-MEE-rya-ti]?",
          "id": "Can I try it on?",
          "literal": "allowed — to-try-on?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Продавчиня:",
          "text": "[Звичайно|Zvi-CHAI-no]. [Примірочна|Pri-MEE-roch-na] [там|tam].",
          "id": "Of course. The fitting room is over there.",
          "literal": "of-course. fitting-room — there."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Ані:",
          "text": "[Дякую|DYA-koo-yoo]... [Цей|Tsey] [гарний|HAR-niy]. [Скільки|SKEEL'-ki] [коштує|KOSH-too-yeh]?",
          "id": "Thank you... This one's nice. How much is it?",
          "literal": "thank-you... this-one (m) — nice. how-much — costs?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Продавчиня:",
          "text": "[Вісімсот|Vee-seem-SOT] [гривень|HRI-ven'].",
          "id": "Eight hundred hryvnias.",
          "literal": "eight-hundred — hryvnias."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Ані:",
          "text": "[Беру|Beh-ROO]. [Він|Veen] [теплий|TEP-liy] [і|ee] [красивий|kra-SI-viy].",
          "id": "I'll take it. It's warm and pretty.",
          "literal": "I-take. he — warm — and — pretty."
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        "**An adjective always follows the gender, number, and case of the noun it describes.** *Новий светр* (m), *нова книга* (f), *нове вікно* (n), *нові книги* (pl). No adjective may keep its dictionary ending when it's attached to a noun.",
        "**The basic endings are -ий, -а, -е, -і.** This is the biggest and easiest group: *гарний, гарна, гарне, гарні*; *великий, велика, велике, великі*; *теплий, тепла, тепле, теплі*.",
        "**A small soft group ends in -ій, -я, -є, -і.** *Синій, синя, синє, сині*. It has few members, but they're common: *синій* (blue), *останній* (last), *сьогоднішній* (today's), *домашній* (homemade). ⚠️ Notice that *синій* and *зелений* behave differently even though both are colors.",
        "**Який? changes too, because it's an adjective itself.** *Який колір?* (m), *Яка сукня?* (f), *Яке пальто?* (n), *Які штани?* (pl). It asks what something is like, not which one from a list; for that people say *котрий*.",
        "**Comparisons are made with -ший or більш.** *Великий* → *більший* (bigger), *маленький* → *менший* (smaller), *гарний* → *гарніший* (nicer). For long words: *більш цікавий* (more interesting). For the most: add **най-**, as in *найбільший* (biggest), *найкращий* (best).",
        "**Поміряти = to try on.** This word is only for clothes and shoes; to try food people use *спробувати*. The full sentence is *Можна поміряти?*: three words that handle the whole fitting-room business.",
        "**Беру = I'll take it, meaning I'll buy it.** Just like English \"I'll take it\". The basic form is *брати*, and it's irregular: *беру, береш, бере, беремо, берете, беруть*."
      ],
